  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The current economic situation in Lebanon, which has been deteriorating quickly over the past few years, has led to many industrial company closures. Investment in the industrial sector in Lebanon has gone down to its lowest level. These external factors negatively affect the Association of Lebanese Industrialists (ALI) ability to attract or retain enterprises.
Despite the crisis, ALI has managed to maintain and even slightly increase the number of members. &#x2013; total number 850. The increase is mainly due to better data management, the implementation of some successful recruitment campaigns and the establishment of new services and benefits to members.  
The institutional assessment conducted with ILO support identified the need to support ALI for meeting its members&#x2019; needs.  Hence, it is essential to conduct a financial and membership strategy aiming at re-balancing and diversifying its resources (including adjusting membership fees, reaching new members, developing or improving new added value services and identifying new incomes sources also at international level. 
During the biennium, ILO will support ALI to be able to enhance service provision in a sustainable way and with a focus on increasing membership outreach. In addition to, adapting or enhancing its services to serve members and non-members (SMEs Development Helpdesk, Export promotion, skills development, research or circular economy and Energy efficiency advice).</narrative>
  </description>
